+## Reliability checks
+
+Reliability work is kept executable alongside the product:
+
+- The Worker test suite covers Git smart-HTTP streaming, mirror failover chaos,
+  state pins, release artifact integrity, private repositories, ActivityPub,
+  bounty payout idempotency, frontend contracts, and performance budgets.
+- The Qt `check` target covers crypto and stores, agent transports, the real
+  application window, startup/tab performance budgets, and a deterministic
+  publish → browse → clone → issue → agent PR → merge loop.
+- The deployment workflow runs the Worker suite before upload and verifies the
+  deployed revision afterward.
+- The public status surface and opt-in desktop telemetry expose availability,
+  host presence, errors, crashes, and GUI stalls.
+
+These checks establish repeatable behavior; they are not a claim that a pre-1.0
+network cannot fail. When documentation and behavior disagree, please open an
+issue under [`.forkmesh/issues/`](.forkmesh/issues/) or submit a focused fix.
+
+## Security model
+
+- Git repositories remain on desktop nodes; the mainnode coordinates routes and
+  streams without becoming the canonical Git store.
+- Signed actions use Ed25519 node identities. Owner push tokens bind repository,
+  operation, identity, and timestamp.
+- Chat payloads are AES-256-GCM encrypted before relay transport. Default rooms
+  use a shared application key; passphrase rooms use a participant-shared key.
+- The private-mirror crypto module encrypts archive content and wraps its key
+  separately for each recipient using X25519 + ML-KEM-768; integration with the
+  normal mirror workflow is still pending.
+- Release downloads are content addressed and checked against sha256 metadata.
+
+Please report vulnerabilities privately using [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).
